  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">EDU: Research in Education for Transformative Opportunities (RETO)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(USAID Latin America and Caribbean Regional):  Research in Education for Transformative Opportunities (RETO) supports key stakeholders in El Salvador, Guatemala and Honduras to more effectively design, implement, and evaluate education programs and policies that contribute to the prevention of youth violence and insecurity. A secure Western Hemisphere is a USG goal made explicit in the U.S. Strategy for Addressing the Root Causes of Migration in Central America, and violence prevention is a development objective in the country-level strategy documents across the Northern Triangle missions. Education programming for youth is part of a multifaceted approach to violence prevention, though a clearer understanding of what works and support with implementing it has been missing in the past. By increasing the quality and relevance of information on education programming for youth violence prevention, RETO helps improve evidence-based decision making among key education stakeholders, thus helping to ensure that investments in improving education are impactful, cost-effective and sustainable, therefore also working to achieve the JRS goal of a prosperous hemisphere through strengthened health and education systems and improved inclusive access. .With FY 2022 funds, RETO will build on the comprehensive education stakeholder maps and evidence gaps maps it has developed by synthesizing and disseminating existing evidence to share with key education stakeholders. They will also work with key stakeholders to collectively turn evidence into action through programs and policies. This will include a collaborative process for strengthening capacity and systems in the region to ensure the use of evidence for decision making well into the future. Finally, they will continue to work with youth by providing internships, building their capacity to synthesize evidence, elevating their voices on violence prevention, and providing youth advocacy training....</narrative>
  </description>
